  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe address of the pair created by the createPair() function in GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol and the pair address predicted by the pairFor() function in Launchpad.sol may not match.\n\n### Description\nThe createPair() function in GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol uses four addresses to calculate the salt value, whereas the pairFor() function in Launchpad.sol uses only two addresses for the same calculation. \nConsequently, the pair addresses computed by these two functions can never match.\n```solidity\n//GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\nfunction createPair(address tokenA, address tokenB) external returns (address pair) {\n\t...\n        bytes32 salt = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1, _launchpadLp, _launchpadFeeDistributor));\n\t...\n    }\n```\n\n```solidity\n//Launchpad.sol\nfunction pairFor(address factory, address tokenA, address tokenB) internal view returns (IUniswapV2Pair pair) {\n        (address token0, address token1) = sortTokens(tokenA, tokenB);\n        pair = IUniswapV2Pair(\n            address(\n                uint160(\n                    uint256(\n                        keccak256(\n                            abi.encodePacked(\n                                hex\"ff\",\n                                factory,\n                                keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1)), //mention\n                                uniV2InitCodeHash // init code hash\n                            )\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        );\n    }\n```\n\n### Impact\n\nWhen the totalFeeShare of a launchToken becomes zero, the endRewards() function in Launchpad.sol is called. \nIn this function, pairFor() is used to predict the pair address. However, since the predicted address will not match the actual deployed pair address, the function will attempt to interact with a non-existent contract, leading to a revert. \nThis failure prevents the endRewards functionality from being executed correctly.\n```solidity\n//Launchpad.sol\nfunction endRewards() external onlyLaunchAsset {\n        address quote = _launches[msg.sender].quote;\n        // @todo stick with one pair interface\n        IGTELaunchpadV2Pair pair = IGTELaunchpadV2Pair(address(pairFor(address(uniV2Factory), msg.sender, quote)));\n\n        distributor.endRewards(pair);\n    }\n```\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nThe pairFor() function in launchpad.sol should calculate the salt using the same four addresses that are used in the createPair() function of GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol.",
  "proof_of_concept": "This issue can be demonstrated using the provided test_CheckPairAddress() function.\n\nLogs:\n  created_pair_addr 0xdB52D3ecEcF767BFBaE5b6638C26afF4dc4ce369\n  invalid : predicted_pair_addr_in_launchpad 0xfa11cE20bE672922eA17E83B1251E28380D89d24\n  valid : predicted_pair_addr 0xdB52D3ecEcF767BFBaE5b6638C26afF4dc4ce369\n\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.27;\n\nimport {Launchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/Launchpad.sol\";\nimport {ILaunchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/ILaunchpad.sol\";\nimport {SimpleBondingCurve} from \"contracts/launchpad/BondingCurves/SimpleBondingCurve.sol\";\nimport {IBondingCurveMinimal} from \"contracts/launchpad/BondingCurves/IBondingCurveMinimal.sol\";\nimport {LaunchToken} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchToken.sol\";\nimport {LaunchpadLPVault} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchpadLPVault.sol\";\nimport {IDistributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IDistributor.sol\";\nimport {Distributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2Pair} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/launchpad/libraries/RewardsTracker.sol\";\nimport {ERC20} from \"@solady/tokens/ERC20.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC1967Factory} from \"@solady/utils/ERC1967Factory.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"../harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\n\nimport {MockUniV2Router} from \"../mocks/MockUniV2Router.sol\";\nimport {MockDistributor} from \"../mocks/MockDistributor.sol\";\n\nimport {FixedPointMathLib} from \"@solady/utils/FixedPointMathLib.sol\";\nimport {ICLOBManager} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOBManager.sol\";\nimport {IOperatorPanel} from \"contracts/utils/interfaces/IOperatorPanel.sol\";\n\nimport {UniV2Bytecode} from \"./integration/UniV2Bytecode.t.sol\";\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\ncontract LaunchpadTest is Test {\n    using FixedPointMathLib for uint256;\n\n    ERC1967Factory factory;\n    Launchpad launchpad;\n    GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory v2Factory;\n    Distributor distributor;\n    IBondingCurveMinimal curve;\n    LaunchpadLPVault launchpadLPVault;\n\n    ERC20Harness quoteToken;\n    MockUniV2Router uniV2Router;\n\n    address owner = makeAddr(\"owner\");\n    address user = makeAddr(\"user\");\n    address dev = makeAddr(\"dev\");\n    address user1 = makeAddr(\"user1\");\n\n    uint256 constant MIN_BASE_AMOUNT = 100_000_000;\n\n    address token;\n\n    uint256 BONDING_SUPPLY;\n    uint256 TOTAL_SUPPLY;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        quoteToken = new ERC20Harness(\"Quote\", \"QTE\");\n\n        factory = new ERC1967Factory();\n\n        address uniV2Factory = makeAddr(\"factory\");\n        vm.etch(uniV2Factory, UniV2Bytecode.UNIV2_FACTORY);\n\n        bytes32 launchpadSalt = bytes32(abi.encode(\"GTE.V1.TESTNET.LAUNCHPAD\", owner));\n        launchpad = Launchpad(factory.predictDeterministicAddress(launchpadSalt));\n\n        address c_logic = address(new SimpleBondingCurve(address(launchpad)));\n        address v_logic = address(new LaunchpadLPVault());\n\n        curve = SimpleBondingCurve(factory.deploy(address(c_logic), owner));\n        launchpadLPVault = LaunchpadLPVault(factory.deploy(address(v_logic), owner));\n\n        address clobManager = makeAddr(\"clob manager\");\n        address operatorAddr = makeAddr(\"operator\");\n        vm.mockCall(\n            operatorAddr,\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(IOperatorPanel.getOperatorRoleApprovals.selector, user, address(0)),\n            abi.encode(0)\n        );\n\n        vm.startPrank(owner);\n        distributor = new Distributor();\n        distributor.initialize(address(launchpad));\n\n        address f_logic = address(new GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory(address(this), address(launchpad), address(launchpad), address(distributor)));\n        v2Factory = GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory(factory.deploy(address(f_logic), owner));\n        uniV2Router = new MockUniV2Router(address(v2Factory));\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        vm.label(address(distributor), \"MOCK_DISTRIBUTOR\");\n\n        address l_logic =\n            address(new Launchpad(address(uniV2Router), address(0), clobManager, operatorAddr, address(distributor)));\n\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        Launchpad(\n            factory.deployDeterministicAndCall({\n                implementation: l_logic,\n                admin: owner,\n                salt: launchpadSalt,\n                data: abi.encodeCall(\n                    Launchpad.initialize,\n                    (\n                        owner,\n                        address(quoteToken),\n                        address(curve),\n                        address(launchpadLPVault),\n                        abi.encode(200_000_000 ether, 10 ether)\n                    )\n                )\n            })\n        );\n\n        token = _launchToken();\n\n        BONDING_SUPPLY = curve.bondingSupply(token);\n        TOTAL_SUPPLY = curve.totalSupply(token);\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(launchpad), type(uint256).max);\n        ERC20Harness(token).approve(address(launchpad), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function _launchToken() internal returns (address) {\n        uint256 fee = launchpad.launchFee();\n        deal(dev, 30 ether);\n\n        vm.prank(dev);\n        return launchpad.launch{value: fee}(\"TestToken\", \"TST\", \"https://testtoken.com\");\n    }\n\n    function pairForInLaunchpad(address factory_addr, address tokenA, address tokenB, bytes32 uniV2InitCodeHash) internal view returns (address pair) {\n        (address token0, address token1) = sortTokens(tokenA, tokenB);\n\n        pair =\n            address(\n                uint160(\n                    uint256(\n                        keccak256(\n                            abi.encodePacked(\n                                hex\"ff\",\n                                factory_addr,\n                                keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1)),\n                                uniV2InitCodeHash\n                            )\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n            );\n    }\n\n    function pairFor(address factory_addr, address tokenA, address tokenB, address _launchpadLp, address _launchpadFeeDistributor, bytes32 uniV2InitCodeHash) internal view returns (address pair) {\n        (address token0, address token1) = sortTokens(tokenA, tokenB);\n\n        pair =\n            address(\n                uint160(\n                    uint256(\n                        keccak256(\n                            abi.encodePacked(\n                                hex\"ff\",\n                                factory_addr,\n                                keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1, _launchpadLp, _launchpadFeeDistributor)),\n                                uniV2InitCodeHash\n                            )\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n            );\n    }\n\n    // returns sorted token addresses, used to handle return values from pairs sorted in this order\n    function sortTokens(address tokenA, address tokenB) internal pure returns (address token0, address token1) {\n        if (tokenA == tokenB) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: IDENTICAL_ADDRESSES\");\n        (token0, token1) = tokenA < tokenB ? (tokenA, tokenB) : (tokenB, tokenA);\n        if (token0 == address(0)) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: ZERO_ADDRESS\");\n    }\n\n    function test_CheckPairAddress() public {\n        vm.startPrank(address(launchpad));\n        address created_pair_addr = v2Factory.createPair(address(token), address(quoteToken));\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        bytes32 uniV2InitCodeHash = keccak256(type(GTELaunchpadV2Pair).creationCode);\n        \n        address predicted_pair_addr_in_launchpad = pairForInLaunchpad(address(v2Factory), address(token), address(quoteToken), uniV2InitCodeHash); \n        address predicted_pair_addr = pairFor(address(v2Factory), address(token), address(quoteToken), address(launchpad), address(distributor), uniV2InitCodeHash); \n\n        console.log(\"created_pair_addr\", created_pair_addr);       \n        console.log(\"invalid : predicted_pair_addr_in_launchpad\", predicted_pair_addr_in_launchpad);       \n        console.log(\"valid : predicted_pair_addr\", predicted_pair_addr);\n    }\n}\n```",
